{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed","id":1422311,"title":"A question of speed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-06T15:45:05-08:00","id":1422311,"title":"A question of speed","content":"What's the fastest a PC Exalt can travel in 3E, canon?<br /> <br /> The best I've got is a Lesser Elemental Dragon (Fakharu, Corebook page 521; or One with the Blue Dragon, Mela's Coil, Arms of the Chosen p107) with its Soaring Dragon Flight merit with a Solar rider using the Charm 'Wind-Racing Essence Infusion' (Core p380) for a journey that would usually take a week.<br /> <br /> That gets you to a speed of 3500 mph.<br /> <br /> If the journey would usually take less than a week, the speed drops to 3000 mph.<br /> <br /> If the rider is an Essence 5 Dragon-Blooded (using Seven-League Gallop) then it's 2500 miles in a single hour, or (regardless of Essence score) 1000 mph for longer journies.<br /> <br /> I don't think anything else comes close to that. An Agata with Wind-Racing Essence Infusion is 210 mph for a week-long journey (180mph for a shorter journey), or 150 miles in a single hour with Seven-League Gallop for a Deeb at Essence 5 (or 60mph otherwise). Stormwind Rider is 100 mph. Wings of the Raptor (four dot artifact) are capped at 80 mph. Chariot of Aerial Conquest (5 dot FAA) is 30 mph.<br /> <br /> Have I missed anything? Anything in the Lunar Charmset?<br /> <br /> I will update the table below as folks add their own Fastest Methods of Travel. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Method</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Speed</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Notes</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Travel Without Distance</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">36,000 mph</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">First 50 miles in an hour only (i.e. 50mph for journies over 50 miles, and not quite as fast for journies under 50 miles).</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Ascendant Nova Phoenix</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">20,000 miles</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Capstone: Reach any point in creation in 1 hour or less (Creation is 20,000 miles long on the diagonal)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Lesser Elemental Dragon</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3,500 mph</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Solar rider, see above</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Ascendant Nova Phoenix</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2,500 mph</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Warstrider, Essence 5, high-altitude cruising speed only, carries 5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Lesser Elemental Dragon</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1,000 mph</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dragon-Blooded rider, 2500 mph over short distances at Essence 5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Lesser Elemental Dragon</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">500 mph</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Base speed (One With The Blue Dragon)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Agata</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">210 mph</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Solar rider, see above</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Stormwind Rider</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">100 mph</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Flat speed, available at Essence 1 to sorcerers.</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-08-2021, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T15:50:17-08:00","id":1422315,"title":"","content":"Well, there's Travel Without Distance that lets you go 50 miles in a matter of seconds if you're Essence 5. If it takes 5 seconds to cast that's about 36,000 miles per hour. If you have a circle of sorcerers who know this spell as their control you could chain them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T16:02:19-08:00","id":1422319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422315#post1422315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there's Travel Without Distance that lets you go 50 miles in a matter of seconds if you're Essence 5. If it takes 5 seconds to cast that's about 36,000 miles per hour. If you have a circle of sorcerers who know this spell as their control you could chain them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately not true: you can't chain it. You can't cast whilst you suffer the fatigue penalty, which lasts at least an hour and applies to passengers as well as the caster.<br /> <br /> So it's 50 miles an hour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T16:09:09-08:00","id":1422321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422319#post1422319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately not true: you can't chain it. You can't cast whilst you suffer the fatigue penalty, which lasts at least an hour and applies to passengers as well as the caster.<br /> <br /> So it's 50 miles an hour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh right the passengers get the fatigue and thus can't cast it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T16:26:26-08:00","id":1422324,"title":"","content":"That Royal Warstrider has an evocation to speed to any part of the world in a relatively short time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T16:39:17-08:00","id":1422325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422324#post1422324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That Royal Warstrider has an evocation to speed to any part of the world in a relatively short time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah Warstriders!<br /> <br /> There are a few with high-speed powers... 30 mph on Emerald Chevalier, 100 mph on Godspeed Vanguard, but I think you mean Ascendant Nova Phoenix which is up to 2500 mph (or six range bands in one turn). I don't see a &quot;speed to any part of the world in a relatively short time&quot; power on any of them though... am I just failing to find this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-06-2020, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T17:06:34-08:00","id":1422331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422325#post1422325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see a &quot;speed to any part of the world in a relatively short time&quot; power on any of them though... am I just dyslexiaing this?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's something in the pinnacle evocation, the Essence 5, one right before Karvara.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T17:07:28-08:00","id":1422333,"title":"","content":"It seems tame by comparison but Stormwind Rider is a flat 100mph","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T17:14:40-08:00","id":1422337,"title":"","content":"[Edit] Cheerfully withdrawn.<br /> <br /> But, yes, I do have severe dyslexia if anyone was wondering. I get my money's worth out of Grammarly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-06-2020, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T17:23:00-08:00","id":1422340,"title":"","content":"I took about a minute to strike that part because it seemed inappropriate without knowing one way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T17:35:30-08:00","id":1422343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422333#post1422333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems tame by comparison but Stormwind Rider is a flat 100mph</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Mortals can cast it though (even if it only lasts an hour per cast for them).<br /> <br /> Solars can get it as one Charm.<br /> Just as fast for Deebs as for Solars.<br /> <br /> I've added to the list, but that's the slowest thing that's making the cut. You must be at least as fast as Stormwind Rider to play.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> I think Isator Levi has the right of it with Ascendant Nova Phoenix's capstone. I would be surprised if there were anything faster than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T17:45:53-08:00","id":1422347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422343#post1422343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Isator Levi has the right of it with Ascendant Nova Phoenix's capstone. I would be surprised if there were anything faster than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found it a bit odd at first, but came to think of it in terms of rapid response to crisis.<br /> <br /> I'm sure it's the fastest thing yet published and might not be exceeded by a written thing, but establishes a standard for powers that might be at least as fast or a bit better, including how they play out and what is necessary for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T18:22:38-08:00","id":1422353,"title":"","content":"One of the Evocations Lady Kratz the Astrologer unlocked from the Emissary's Mask in my Sunday game lets her teleport instantaneously from one person to another along the threads where their destinies meet. It's somewhat limited in that she has to be aware of the relationship between them, and moreover each subject has to have an Intimacy for the other.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut since the thread topic insists on canon, I can't think of anything faster than Ascendant Nova Phoenix's capstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T01:01:17-08:00","id":1422394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422353#post1422353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the Evocations Lady Kratz the Astrologer unlocked from the Emissary's Mask in my Sunday game lets her teleport instantaneously from one person to another along the threads where their destinies meet. It's somewhat limited in that she has to be aware of the relationship between them, and moreover each subject has to have an Intimacy for the other.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut since the thread topic insists on canon, I can't think of anything faster than Ascendant Nova Phoenix's capstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I made this it's own topic specifically so we could go down tangents like this.<br /> <br /> Would you be willing to discuss the themes and other Charms of Emissary's Mask? What's it made of? Where did it come from? What powers lead upto this teleportation one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T03:11:09-08:00","id":1422403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422394#post1422394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you be willing to discuss the themes and other Charms of Emissary's Mask?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422394#post1422394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's it made of?</div> </div> </div> </div>The outside is silver. Inside, a special gold glass, created by layering sorcerous orichalcum between lenses of glass surgically removed from two of the floating eyes of Orabilis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422394#post1422394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did it come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Once, in the Celestial City, the goddess Shalrina was visited by the Exalted lord of a distant city. He sought her assistance in creating a unique artifact that he could grant to one of the mortals employed in his bureaucracy: a mask that would empower the wearer to serve the city.<br /> <br /> Shalrina agreed to do this thing, and traveled with him to his city, but realized halfway through the endeavor of crafting the mask that she had been deceived; the design of the mask would indeed imbue the wearer with unique power, but also enslave them to the will of the lord. <br /> <br /> Enraged by the deception, Shalrina sabotaged the mask in a subtle way; its wearer would <i>appear</i> to be loyal to the Exalted lord, but their ultimate allegiance would be to a group of mortals.<br /> <br /> The tyrannical lord was unaware of her careful treason; the day after his Emissary donned the mask, the goddess told some mortals oppressed by his rule how they might command the Emissary.<br /> <br /> It was wise that she returned to Yu-Shan in the hours following that, because the battle between Exalt and Emissary was vicious enough to reduce the city to a smoking ruin. <br /> <br /> One day, a sorcerer stopped his travels to rest in the ruins of the city and take shelter from the storm. When he awoke the next morning, the rain had washed some of the rubble clear, and he saw a glint of silver\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422394#post1422394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What powers lead upto this teleportation one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each person to wear the mask gets a pseudo-Excellency, and a unique set of Evocations. <br /> <br /> In Lady Kratz\u2019s case, for example, she can spend a mote to succeed on her Read Intentions action against a person to know their goal for the scene if she\u2019s read their destiny via her astrology (which is itself mechanically identical to the Reading the Tea Leaves ritual), ignore environmental penalties to track a person by following their thread of fate, create phantom \u201cechoes\u201d to assist in a Case Scene action, and the aforementioned teleportation. <br /> <br /> When Brueghel was wearing the mask, he could cast sorcery up to the Celestial level, and gained access to a Burning Name-like attack that did aggravated damage, afflicting the target with gruesome, and painful transformations. <br /> <br /> Ephiselle the Midnight Queen can, when wearing the mask, see through the \u201ceyes\u201d of any statue of herself or the Emissary, turn water into agonizing poison, and hear her name or office being spoken anywhere in the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-07-2020, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T05:30:54-08:00","id":1422412,"title":"","content":"I'm away from books at the moment, but the Storm Serpent (I think?) from Hundred Devils has an Eclipse charm that lets you teleport anywhere in the same storm system--at which point speed is a question of &quot;how big a storm can you make?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T12:14:37-08:00","id":1422469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422412#post1422412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm away from books at the moment, but the Storm Serpent (I think?) from Hundred Devils has an Eclipse charm that lets you teleport anywhere in the same storm system--at which point speed is a question of &quot;how big a storm can you make?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Some common storms can reach 20-30km in radius. The biggest known typhoon reached....1<a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4e/Typhoonsizes.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">100km of radius I think</a>? One in the center of the blessed isle would hit both its northern and southern coast at the same time.<br /> <br /> So a storm can get pretty stupidly large. The &quot;usual&quot; big storm is closer to the former, though. It's pretty analog to travel without distance replacing the cooldown with a fixed landing area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T16:02:11-08:00","id":1422507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422412#post1422412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm away from books at the moment, but the Storm Serpent (I think?) from Hundred Devils has an Eclipse charm that lets you teleport anywhere in the same storm system--at which point speed is a question of &quot;how big a storm can you make?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you take <i>Beckoning That Which Stirs the Sky</i> as your control spell, any weather effect you make follows you and lasts for hours. So lets do a little back of then envelope here. <br /> Int 5 Occult 5 Specialty, Full excellency, 2 point stunt, and a willpowers will get you (10+1+10+2)23 dice with 2 auto successes. we can call that, on average, 12 successes. <br /> <br /> Making a typhoon from clear skies is Difficulty 7. which leaves 5 threshold success. It costs half (round up) for it to persist, which means you have 2 remaining threshold successes. You have (Ess 5+Thresh 2) 7 miles radius out from you, and it lasts for (1+thresh 2) hours, 3 hours. The Sorcery has a Ritual cast time of &quot;a few minutes&quot;. So at the max, we can say 5 minutes. <br /> <br /> Adding that up, assuming the Storm Serpent charm doesn't have a reset condition, you can spend 5 minutes to make a 7 mile radius &quot;teleport zone&quot; (94 mph at this stage for 1 jump) and since the weather follows you, and is centered on you, you can now chain jumps as long as you have the resources to do so. assuming 7 miles again, and your turn as being 5 seconds, that second jump is <b>5,040 mph</b>. If you can do this for 3 hours, you will cross <b>15,000 miles</b>, aka 3/4ths of Creation.<br /> <br /> Under ideal conditions though, moving a rainstorm to a typhoon is only diff 2, and if you roll higher and get say, 16 successes then you have 14 threshold (control halves to 7), which makes the second jump 12 miles, <b>8640 mph</b> for 8 hours. or 69,00 miles, more than triple Creations distance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T19:05:16-08:00","id":1422525,"title":"","content":"Something tells me that the bit about the weather following you in the spell didn't take into account the possibility of teleportation. I'd assume that the weather patterns following you would still have to travel at the sorts of speeds that occur naturally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T00:16:21-08:00","id":1422560,"title":"","content":"Also, if you're blowing a full excellency every time, that's 4-8 casts before you're mote-tapped. So... like 40 minutes of travel -- you're not doing this for eight hours.<br /> <br /> Still... it's a fantastic idea. Add in Stormcaller, perhaps, for instant rain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-08-2020, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T01:41:04-08:00","id":1422570,"title":"","content":"Unicorn has a +5 speed bonus, which is the fastest of any creature in 3e.<br /> <br /> Racing is an opposed roll. So if an exalt can roll more successes than an opponent, they are by definition going slightly faster than them. I wonder how many dice a fighter jet rolls when going supersonic?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422525#post1422525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something tells me that the bit about the weather following you in the spell didn't take into account the possibility of teleportation. I'd assume that the weather patterns following you would still have to travel at the sorts of speeds that occur naturally.</div> </div> </div> </div>For contrast, Rain of Doom moves with a control sorcerer at up to 15 miles per hour (Essence x3 mph) .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T05:17:06-08:00","id":1422585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrFamiliar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422570#post1422570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unicorn has a +5 speed bonus, which is the fastest of any creature in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joint fastest with Lesser Elemental Dragons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Racing is an opposed roll. So if an exalt can roll more successes than an opponent, they are by definition going slightly faster than them. I wonder how many dice a fighter jet rolls when going supersonic? </div> </div> </div>A horse is +4. 500 mph on an Elemental Dragon is +5. 10mph on a Unicorn is also +5.<br /> <br /> (I'm also not entirely convinced that you've drawn a logical conclusion there vis opposed rolls, racing and absolute speed. &quot;The Tortious and the Hare&quot; and &quot;Flash vs Superman&quot; come to mind.)<br /> <br /> Ascendant Nova Phoenix is probably the closest example of a fighter jet. High altitude it's flying at just over Mach 3, but it has to slow down to reasonably participate in combat -- at which point it gets 5 bonus dice. I imagine a jet fighter would be the same: it can make an uncontested flyby (much like a Solar making a Difficulty 2 Melee roll to instantly dispatch an ordinary mortal guard), but if it's trading blows back-and-forth then it needs to be operating at back-and-forth relative speeds (+5 Speed Bonus, maybe +6, maybe +4).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For contrast, Rain of Doom moves with a control sorcerer at up to 15 miles per hour (Essence x3 mph) . </div> </div> </div>That's probably a good rule of thumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-08-2020, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T19:20:32-08:00","id":1422683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422560#post1422560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you're blowing a full excellency every time, that's 4-8 casts before you're mote-tapped. So... like 40 minutes of travel -- you're not doing this for eight hours.<br /> <br /> Still... it's a fantastic idea. Add in Stormcaller, perhaps, for instant rain?</div> </div> </div> </div>You only blow an Excellency to summon the storm. I have no idea how the Eclipse Charm works though. RAW the storm is always follows you (no speed limit) but no sane ST would allow for this level of shenanigans. IRL Hurricanes move 10 to 35 mph though so there's that. <br /> <br /> Although you could use the non-control version and keep summoning NEW storms with full excellency, which at E5 you could do probably 5 or 6 times, which would be 12 miles each every &quot;few minutes&quot;, so with Stormcaller out thats roughly 12 miles in 3 minutes, aka 4 miles per minute or 240 mph. I admit this is very contextual and handwavy though. <br /> <br /> Otoh, if there was a Second Circle Demon of Storms (Like Avadra pre-stormcaller), then maybe it could make a massive Continent sized thunderstorm and you could just teleport anywhere","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T19:27:43-08:00","id":1422686,"title":"","content":"Akavadra's description is very much Third Circle scale, and summoning a storm with thousands of kilometers is definitely outside the second circle's power scale. <br /> <br /> Other than that yeah, you want to bring an apocalypse just to teleport better? Go to town. A storm that big can exist naturally, and it's definitely fitting for such a mighty demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T23:29:22-08:00","id":1422698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422311-a-question-of-speed?p=1422683#post1422683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You only blow an Excellency to summon the storm. I have no idea how the Eclipse Charm works though. RAW the storm is always follows you (no speed limit) but no sane ST would allow for this level of shenanigans. IRL Hurricanes move 10 to 35 mph though so there's that. </div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, now I see.<br /> <br /> I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}